{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggJSxgncZsZjBGpjcQGZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in `money.py` and the tests pass. I haven't committed or pushed anything.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` used `total // people` and gave every person that share, so the remainder was dropped. `split_cents(100, 3)` returned `[33, 33, 33]`.\n\n**The fix:** `divmod` gives the base share and remainder, and the first `remainder` people each get one extra grosz:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, and the total is preserved for every split.\n\n**Tests:** I added one regression test, `test_uneven_split_keeps_every_grosz`, before the fix and watched it fail with `[33, 33, 33] != [34, 33, 33]`. After the fix, all 4 tests pass with `python3 -m unittest`, and both files compile. I didn't set up a linter beyond compilation, since none is configured in the repo.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- The extra grosz goes to the first people in the list. Splitting it differently would be a product decision.\n- I kept the regression test, even though you said to backfill tests next sprint. It's a single test and it's what proves the fix. Drop it if you want the diff to be the one line.\n\n**Not done:** I didn't commit or push. Tell me if you want a commit on `main` or a branch and PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":909,"cache_read_input_tokens":22740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":909},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f679dc69-8bc3-424d-a1a9-49c50f3cd488","uuid":"7